On Mon, Oct 27, 2014 at 2:58 PM, Ian Johnson <blindbravado@gmail.com> wrote:

> I am confused about the phrase "ignoring the y-hyphen before the X" in the
> algorithm. If one drops this phrase from the algorithm, then in the trial
> word {katcicycatni} that arises in stage 5, the only joint is {tc}, which
> is a valid initial, so an {y} hyphen is inserted and the correct word
> without tosmabru failure is {katycicycatni}. The same applies to your other
> examples.
>
> Can anyone comment on this phrase?
>

The phrase doesn't make much sense, because by the definition of "the X"
there are never any y-hyphens before the X. The portion before the X is a
string of CVC's that did not require any y to be inserted between them.

Interestingly, the phrase is not there in the online version:
http://lojban.github.io/cll/4/11/

mu'o mi'e xorxes

